# Orders (planned — not built)

**Do not start this work yet.** Phases 0–4 (through manager catalog) are done. Branch orders wait for Phase 5 (`branches` app + internal request). Stock already exists (goods receipt ledger); that is not a reason to start orders now.

The `branches` app is **not built**. Design only: @docs/warehouse-tenancy-setup.md

## Already in place (warehouse, not tenancy)

- `accounts.User` — email login
- Global `Item` catalogue (no `branch_id`)
- Stock ledger: `StockMovement` + cached `Item.quantity`

## Not in place (do not assume these exist)

- `Branch`, `BranchMembership`
- `branches/permissions.py`
- `request.active_branch`

## Order phase rules (when the phase actually starts)

- Do **not** implement the historical `item_name` / `quantity` / `notes` stub in the tenancy doc
- Every `Order` has required `branch` FK and `created_by` FK
- Order lines should reference `Item` (snapshot description/price later)
- Always query orders via branch-scoped manager (e.g. `.for_user_branches(user)`)
- Role checks at view entry using future `branches/permissions.py`
- Client-side order IDs for idempotent sync (offline retries)
- Catalogue stays global (no `branch_id` on `Item`)
